# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your project's SDK setup:
# Project settings → General → Your apps → SDK setup and configuration → Config
# https://console.firebase.google.com/project/_/settings/general
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ variables are inlined into the JavaScript bundle at build time.
# Anyone with the app can read them. That is expected for the Firebase config —
# it identifies your project rather than granting access to it. What actually
# guards your data is database.rules.json and storage.rules.
#
# What must never appear in this file: a service account JSON, a Firebase Admin
# SDK private key, or an OAuth *client secret*. Those belong in server-side
# environment variables only.

EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyYour_Api_Key_Here
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project-id.firebaseapp.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
# Projects created before October 2024 use `your-project-id.appspot.com` here.
# Copy whatever the console shows rather than assuming the suffix.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project-id.firebasestorage.app
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=000000000000
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:0000000000000000000000

# ── Realtime Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A HOST, not an id. `getDatabase(app, 'default')` parses its second argument
# as a URL and fails with "Cannot parse Firebase url" — there is no id→URL
# lookup in the client SDK, so the URL has to be given outright.
#
# Since ~2023 new instances use a REGIONAL host, so the old
#   https://<db>.firebaseio.com
# shape usually 404s and the real value is
#   https://<db>.<region>.firebasedatabase.app
# Copy it verbatim from Build → Realtime Database (the console shows the URL at
# the top). For this project:
#   https://election-managment-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app
#
# One-line check, no auth needed:
#   200 + `null`  → instance exists and is empty
#   401 PERMISSION_DENIED → instance exists, rules are doing their job
#   404 (empty body)      → wrong host / no instance
#
# Free tier (Spark) is enough: 1 GB stored, 10 GB/month downloaded, 100
# concurrent connections. Note the free tier is single-region and this SDK
# version has no offline disk cache, same as Firestore here.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=https://<db-name>.<region>.firebasedatabase.app

# ── Campaign HQ (admin panel) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required for creating accounts from the mobile app.
#
# A Firebase custom claim can only be written with the Admin SDK, so after the
# app creates the Auth user + profile it calls Campaign HQ's
# /api/account/claims route to put the role on the new login's token. Without
# this URL the create form refuses to start: it will not leave behind an
# account the rules treat as roleless.
#
# Use the admin panel's ORIGIN — no trailing slash and no /api suffix:
#   https://your-campaign-hq.vercel.app
#
# Local development: `localhost` means the phone itself on a physical device,
# and the Android emulator needs 10.0.2.2. Use the computer's LAN address:
#   http://192.168.1.20:3000
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMIN_API_URL=https://your-campaign-hq.vercel.app

# ── Google sign-in ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Three OAuth clients from the Google Cloud project your Firebase project owns
# (APIs & Services → Credentials). The Google button stays hidden until the web
# client ID *and* the one for the current platform are both set.
#
# These are client IDs, not secrets — they are public by design.
#
# WEB is load-bearing on native too, not only on web: Firebase lists it under
# the Google provider's "Web SDK configuration", and the ID token's `aud` claim
# must match it or signInWithCredential rejects the credential.
#
# Google sign-in needs a development build. expo-auth-session's hosted proxy was
# removed in SDK 48, so under Expo Go the redirect is `exp://…`, which no Google
# client type accepts.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-xxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-xxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=000000000000-xxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ── Email link sign-in and in-app password reset ─────────────────────────
# An https URL on a domain listed under Authentication → Settings → Authorized
# domains. A custom scheme (myapp://) is rejected.
#
# Leave this unset and both flows still work: the reset link opens Firebase's
# own hosted page in a browser, and the "Email me a link instead" button is
# hidden. Set it — and claim the domain with Universal Links / App Links, and
# build — and both come back into the app instead.
#
# Firebase Dynamic Links shut down on 25 August 2025; a Firebase Hosting domain
# plus associated domains is the supported replacement. See the README.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_LINK_URL=https://your-project-id.firebaseapp.com/finish-sign-in

# Set to 1 to point the app at `npm run emulators` instead of your real
# project. Leave it unset — or anything other than 1 — for the cloud.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_USE_EMULATOR=1
